318: 
319: **Weeks.** Grades 9 to 12 have no stagger rule but the finals week (docs/courses/CALENDAR.md rule 4; the after-core
320: brief lets a 6 to 12 year-end check sit in week 32), and these checks also keep off the core course-level check
321: weeks of each grade as CALENDAR.md shows them today: grade 9 weeks 9, 10, 12, 13, 16, 18, 19, 20 and 22; grade 10
322: weeks 8, 9, 10, 11, 18, 19, 20 and 21; grade 11 weeks 10, 13, 14, 15, 16, 19, 22, 23 and 24; grade 12 weeks 8, 9,
323: 10, 11, 15, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 23, 24, 25 and 30 (week 32 is every course's finals week). So the mid-year checks
324: sit in week 17 in grades 9, 10 and 11 and week 16 in grade 12 (week 17 holds grade 12's ELA, Calculus and US History
325: II checks), and every year-end check sits in week 32. That is why each year's last unit (9, 18, 27 and 36) ends on
326: day 157 with its own end-of-unit assessment and the year-end check follows it; the check draws its items from the
327: earlier units, so the cost is stated plainly: the ids of units 9 (SS Argue), 18 (SS Argue), 27 (MA Argue) and 36
328: (LA Argue, owner year) are checked in their year by their end-of-unit assessment only; grade 9, 10 and 11's are
329: checked again in the next year's checks through the matching unit, and unit 36's record goes to the school's team.
330: Owned rows every check samples: all others. `frame.py calendar` lists these weeks beside other after-core checks;
331: the weeks stay until the lead's calendar pass across the after-core frames.
332: 
333: **How a check runs in 45 minutes.** The interpretive parts (the teacher reads the new text aloud once, students
334: read it again themselves) and the writing task go to the whole class at once; the talk task is heard in small
335: seminars of three, about six minutes a group with the teacher listening, while the others write, over the two days.
336: Each student is heard once in a check. The respond day groups students by form and by entry point (at most four
337: groups; the others rehearse in pairs from the frame). No scores are stored; the teacher's paper sheet stays with
338: the teacher (promise 2).
