## Seams

### Picked up from English Language Development, grades 6 to 8

Grade 8 hands on all 13 rows (data/progressions/eld.csv, the grade 8 rows' hands_on), and grade 9 picks each up as a
retrieval task on day 2 of the unit that first needs it. Every model moves from the 6 to 8 stage to the 9 to 12
stage here.

| Grade 8 hands on | Row that picks it up | Unit here | What grade 9 does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| g8-si-narrate | g9-si-narrate | 1 | The newsletter recount for an absent reader becomes one event told twice, for a peer and an adult, with tense shifts and reflective language; the newsletter frame is gone for 3 and 4 |
| g8-la-narrate | g9-la-narrate | 1 | Point of view and episodes grow into structure across time: a scene with one time shift |
| g8-sc-explain; g8-si-explain | g9-sc-explain; g9-si-explain | 2 | Explanations link structure and function; one's own reasoning is explained in seminar, so hedging is new |
| g8-ma-explain | g9-ma-explain | 3 | Each step of an equation is justified, and what a graph's slope and intercept mean |
| g8-sc-argue; g8-si-argue | g9-sc-argue; g9-si-argue | 4 | Claims draw on several lines of evidence with a limit named; changing one's view for a good reason is taught as a strength |
| g8-ma-argue | g9-ma-argue | 5 | Claims rest on data and definitions: correlation or causation, linear or exponential |
| g8-la-argue | g9-la-argue | 6 | Evaluating an argument's reasoning, with concession and hedging modals |
| g8-la-inform; g8-si-inform | g9-la-inform; g9-si-inform | 7 | Analysis of how a whole text's ideas unfold, joined with clauses; a seminar summed up for a classmate who missed it |
| g8-ss-explain | g9-ss-explain | 8 | Explanations weigh several factors in context |
| g8-ss-argue | g9-ss-argue | 9 | A historical thesis defended with sourced evidence and compared interpretations |

