| g11-sc-argue (unit 25) | g12-sc-argue | 35 | Owner year: a trade-off, uncertainty and a rebuttal |
| g11-la-argue (unit 22) | g12-la-argue | 36 | Owner year: a rebuttal and a concession for a real audience |

Every pick-up above is answered at both ends in data/progressions/eld.csv (each grade 9, 10 and 11 row's hands_on
names the next grade's row of the same skill, and each grade 10, 11 and 12 row's assumes names the row before).

### Where the threads end

Grade 12 is the last ELD year. Every content thread ends in the owner year's unit (28 to 36), checked by a task the
student does alone at levels 3 and 4 from the model with no sentence frame (the row notes' grade 12 withdrawal).
The four SI threads end here too, carried since their owner year, grade 4. The school's own exit score, not this
course, decides when a student leaves English learner status.

## Models carried

All four models are paper sheets the student and teacher fill; they reach the 9 to 12 stage here (the progression's
"Model:" lines) from the 6 to 8 stage of grade 8.

| Model | Where it comes from | Introduced or first used here | Used again here |
|---|---|---|---|
| story map | ELD grades 6 to 8 (g8-la-narrate, model_out, the 6 to 8 stage: point of view and episodes); here the 9 to 12 stage, structure across time | Unit 1 (g9-la-narrate, g9-si-narrate: two time lines) | Unit 3 (SI narrate review: a session in order); unit 13 (two narratives compared); unit 18 (the research path); unit 19 (a structural choice and a reflection); unit 27 (SI narrate review: a study's run); unit 28 (a turning point and resolution, owner year); unit 34 (SI narrate review: a test told with its limits) |
| text map | ELD grades 6 to 8 (g8-la-inform, g8-si-inform, model_out); here the 9 to 12 stage, two or more sources synthesized | Unit 7 (g9-la-inform, g9-si-inform: one text's unfolding ideas and a seminar's speakers) | Unit 9 (SI inform review: two historians side by side); unit 10 (SI inform review: a briefing); unit 17 (two sources); unit 20 (several sources for a named reader); unit 25 (SI inform review: a written request); unit 30 (SI inform review: an orientation); unit 33 (defined terms and synthesis, owner year) |
| cause chain | ELD grades 6 to 8 (g8-sc-explain, g8-ma-explain, g8-ss-explain, g8-si-explain, model_out); here the 9 to 12 stage, weighted causes | Unit 2 (g9-sc-explain, g9-si-explain) | Units 3, 8 (grade 9 explain); units 10, 11, 15 (grade 10); units 21, 23, 26 (grade 11); units 29, 30, 31 (grade 12, weighted and multi-factor, owner year) |
| claim chart | ELD grades 6 to 8 (g8-sc-argue, g8-ma-argue, g8-la-argue, g8-ss-argue, g8-si-argue, model_out); here the 9 to 12 stage, rebuttal and the limits of the evidence | Unit 4 (g9-sc-argue, g9-si-argue) | Units 5, 6, 9 (grade 9); units 12, 14, 16, 18 (grade 10); units 22, 24, 25, 27 (grade 11); units 32, 34, 35, 36 (grade 12, owner year) |

The four models end in grade 12. Sentence frames and word banks are scaffolds, not models (progression read
2026-11-21): they are withdrawn on the days in The course in brief.

