notes: Students recount an experience in school life for a formal audience (a club report, an introduction to a visitor) and an informal one. Entry points (all recount an experience in school life for a formal audience, a club report or an introduction to a visitor, and for an informal one): levels 1 and 2 with the story map and two audience cards, a word bank and the cloze "This year our club ___. One event was ___.", the cloze off before the check and the word bank kept; 3 and 4 with "Over the past term, the club ___. The highlight was ___." beside the informal version, off before the end-of-unit recount; 5 and 6 with the story map only, choosing tone words for each audience, the frame gone after the first application day. Forms: a formal recount (opening, events, highlight, close) beside an informal one; tense shifts on purpose (present for the club now, past for the events) and reflective language; over the past term, the highlight was and on behalf of. Home language: a student may plan both versions in the home language first; the visitor hears English. Carried, owned in grade 4. In grade 10 the formal audience is a real visitor or club, so the opening and close carry the register; the grade 9 two-telling cloze is gone for levels 3 and 4. Teacher note: prompts follow APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground; a home, family or where-you-are-from prompt is one of several, and an invented character or a chosen place is always allowed.

